@title EPISODE 05 • THE FUNDRAISER 5K
@bg downtown_morning
@show diggy
Charity 5K downtown. London and Diggy in matching purple bibs. Little kids keep asking if they're married.
Diggy: Kid number four. You want to answer this one?
London: Tell her we're colleagues.
Diggy: She's six, Sterling.
Mile two. A little boy trips and skins both knees. His mom is way back in the crowd.
> [Sweet] Stop and help him, race be damned. -> k_sweet
> [Bold] "Diggy, carry him. I'll find his mom." -> k_bold
> [Bad] Keep running — somebody else will stop. -> k_bad
*k_sweet
@add Diggy_Affection 3
@add Diggy_Trust 2
You kneel in the street in your $300 running shoes. Diggy watches you like he's seeing you for the first time.
Diggy: Huh.
London: What?
Diggy: Nothing. Just... huh.
@jump k_done
*k_bold
@add Diggy_Trust 2
@add Team_Reputation 2
Teamwork, perfectly. Two minutes later the kid is laughing on Diggy's shoulders. You finish together, last, and somehow it's the best race all year.
@jump k_done
*k_bad
@add Diggy_Affection -2
@add Diggy_Trust -2
You look back once. Diggy stopped. Of course he did. At the finish line he doesn't say a word to you, and that's louder than anything.
*k_done
@bg diner_night
@show diggy
After: a 24-hour diner, because Diggy says real runners eat pancakes after races.
Diggy: Can I ask you something real?
London: Depends how real.
Diggy: Why you act like you hate everybody?
> [Sweet] "...Because if I like people, they can leave." -> d_sweet
> [Bitchy] "I don't act. I'm committed to the role." -> d_bitchy
> [Bold] "Why do YOU act like nothing bothers you?" -> d_bold
*d_sweet
@add Diggy_Trust 3
@add Diggy_Affection 2
@add London_Confidence -1
He doesn't joke. He doesn't push. He just slides the syrup over and says, "I'm not going anywhere. Somebody gotta beat you at the 300."
@jump d_done
*d_bitchy
